  "notes": "Transcribed 2026-11-13 from the official Southern Utah University 2026-2027 General Catalog (current edition, catoid=28) Musical Theatre program page (poid=10928) and its linked official degree map, 'Musical Theatre Degree Maps (2026-2027)', tab 'Musical Theatre (Campus)' (the workbook's Index lists Online as N/A for this program), last updated/reviewed August 3, 2026. Semester placement is the university's official sample 4-year campus academic plan (SUU Program Maps, 2026-2027), which the source itself labels a guide only; students confirm specifics in Degree Works with a Student Success Advisor. Every semester's courses sum to the map's printed semester total (16/15/16/15/13/14/15/16) and the plan to the catalog's printed Total Credits, BFA Degree: 120. Per the catalog, BFA students must maintain a major-level GPA of 3.0 in theatre-based courses and a cumulative GPA of 2.0; admission is by interview and audition before a faculty panel; every student completes an annual interview and performance jury, a significant internship, and a Capstone with a written and oral defense. The catalog's BFA Theatre Core Requirements (27 credits) are exercised exactly (THEA 1033, 1113, 1713, 1813, 2713, 3613, 3713, 3723 as placed, and THEA 4890 Internship at the catalog-required 3 of its 3-12 credits). The Performance Course Requirements (23 credits) are exercised exactly (THEA 4140 Rehearsal and Performance at 1 credit in each of Fall and Spring Year 3, the catalog's 2-credit minimum of its 1-3 range). The Musical Theatre Course Requirements (42 credits) are exercised in total: the Dance Core (8 credits; the catalog assigns an 8-credit dance technique core by placement and advisement and lists no courses) is exercised by the map's four 2-credit 'DANC XXXX (Level)' rows (Jazz, Ballet, Modern, Tap), recorded as choice slots with synthetic codes; the Dance Courses (6) are DANC 1170, 1520, 2070 and 3070 as placed; the Music Theory block (8) is MUSC 1150, 1160, 1110, 1130 and MUSC 1400 at 1 credit twice (the catalog's 'must take 2 times'); and the Theatre Courses (6) are THEA 3133 and 4163 as placed. DISCLOSED, transcribed as printed and not reconciled: the Music Applied Voice Courses block totals 14 credits in both sources, but the map exercises THEA 2411 MT Group Applied Voice at 3 credits (1 in Fall Year 1 and 2 in Spring Year 1) against the catalog's 2 (1 credit, must take 2 times) and THEA 3411 MT Applied Voice at 11 credits (1+2+2+2+2+2 across six terms) against the catalog's 12 (1-2 credits, must take for a total of 12 credits); the two map values are recorded as printed. allow_repeated_courses is set for the printed repeats (THEA 2411, THEA 3411, THEA 4140, MUSC 1400). Catalog course titles are recorded where the map shortens them (e.g. THEA 3723 'Theatre History: Realism, Post-Realistic, and Contemporary Theatre'; THEA 1221 'Make-Up for the Actor'). GE, free-elective and dance-level rows printed without course codes are recorded as choice slots with synthetic codes.",
